Fix kernel panic in __set_task_comm with CONFIG_PERF_HUMANTASK

find_task_by_vpid() was called without RCU protection and without a
NULL check, then parent->comm was dereferenced unconditionally.
When a process setns()es into another PID namespace (DroidSpaces
container start) and execve()s, tsk->tgid cannot be resolved in the
active namespace, so find_task_by_vpid() returns NULL and
strcmp(parent->comm) dereferences NULL + offsetof(task_struct, comm)
= 0x840 (pc __pi_strcmp, lr __set_task_comm, Process [ds-monitor]),
panic and device reboot.

Guard the lookup with rcu_read_lock() and skip the boost when the
parent cannot be resolved or is not system_server. Semantics for the
normal Android case are unchanged.

--- a/fs/exec.c
+++ b/fs/exec.c
@@ -1255,13 +1255,28 @@
 void __set_task_comm(struct task_struct *tsk, const char *buf, bool exec)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_PERF_HUMANTASK
-	struct task_struct *parent = find_task_by_vpid(tsk->tgid);
+	struct task_struct *parent;
 	char *tmpbuf = kmalloc(128, GFP_KERNEL);
 #endif
 	task_lock(tsk);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PERF_HUMANTASK
-	if (!strcmp(parent->comm, "system_server")) {
+	/*
+	 * find_task_by_vpid() must be called under RCU read lock, and it may
+	 * return NULL: after setns() into another PID namespace (e.g. Linux
+	 * containers like DroidSpaces), tsk->tgid is not resolvable in the
+	 * active namespace. Dereferencing parent without a NULL check caused
+	 * a kernel panic (strcmp on parent->comm) on execve inside a
+	 * container. Filter parent under RCU and skip the boost if not
+	 * resolvable or not system_server.
+	 */
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	parent = find_task_by_vpid(tsk->tgid);
+	if (parent && strcmp(parent->comm, "system_server"))
+		parent = NULL;
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	if (parent) {
 		if (!strcmp(buf, "InputDispatcher") ||
 		    !strcmp(buf, "InputReader")) {
 			tsk->human_task = MAX_LEVER + 1;
